## Interface: 16001
## Title: Skwirlert
## Notes: Buff and timer expiration alerts with per-reminder sounds, profiles, share codes, per-member buff tracking, Group Sync, Aspect warnings and an after-combat cure/resurrect check.
## Author: ERitzFoto
## Version: 0.9.3-beta
## SavedVariables: SkwirlertDB
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\Skwirlert\Media\SkwirlertIcon

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# How this file works (for new addon developers):
#   * Lines starting with "##" are metadata WoW reads:
#       Interface      - client version the addon targets (16001 = WoW Forever 1.60.1)
#       SavedVariables - global table(s) WoW saves to disk on logout / reload
#       IconTexture    - icon shown in the AddOns list (path without extension;
#                        Media\SkwirlertIcon.tga, 128x128, 32-bit TGA)
#   * Lines starting with a single "#" are comments.
#   * Every other line is a file to load, IN THIS ORDER. Each .lua file
#     receives the same private namespace table (`local ADDON, ns = ...`), so
#     a file can use anything defined by the files listed above it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Foundation: namespace, profiles, saved data, error capture, event dispatch
Core.lua
# Safe wrappers around game APIs (secret values, buff lookups)
Compat.lua
# Alert sounds, chat announcements, popup box
Sounds.lua
Announce.lua
Popup.lua
# Timers, cast detection and buff verification (decides WHEN to alert)
Engine.lua
# Settings window, "Add from my buffs", share codes, bug reports
Config.lua
BuffPicker.lua
Share.lua
Diagnostics.lua
# Pause Monitoring and the minimap button (0.7.0)
Pause.lua
MinimapButton.lua
# Group Sync: share running timers with groupmates who use Skwirlert (0.8.0)
Sync.lua
# Combat alerts: Aspect warning and the after-combat group check (0.9.0)
CombatAlerts.lua
# Welcome window at login, with "Don't show this again" (0.9.1)
Welcome.lua
# "Loaded" chat line and "a newer version is available" notice (0.9.2)
Version.lua
# /skwirlert slash command
Commands.lua
